%% title: From building a routine to substitute teachers
%% desc: The Admin first sets shifts, period times and rules. Then they arrange each section's routine, send it for review and publish it. In review, teachers see only their own periods; after publishing, everyone sees it. If a teacher is absent, the Admin records a substitute teacher for that day only, and the weekly routine does not change.
flowchart LR
  S["Routine setup<br/>shifts, periods, rules"]:::admin --> B["Class routine<br/>arrange each section"]:::admin
  B --> R["Routine review<br/>Draft → In review"]:::admin
  R --> P["Publish<br/>can't go back"]:::admin
  R -. "In review" .-> T1["Teacher<br/>own periods only"]:::teacher
  P --> T["Teacher<br/>My routine"]:::teacher
  P --> G["Students and guardians<br/>routine in the portal"]:::guardian
  T --> A{"Teacher<br/>absent?"}:::note
  A -- "yes" --> SUB["Substitute teacher<br/>that day only"]:::admin
  SUB --> T
  classDef teacher fill:#e7f5ff,stroke:#1c7ed6,color:#0b3d66
  classDef admin fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7a2e05
  classDef guardian fill:#ebfbee,stroke:#2b8a3e,color:#14411d
  classDef note fill:#f1f3f5,stroke:#868e96,color:#343a40
